# Finish waypoint

Shared is the **gate**, not the finish line. Target = working end-to-end.

## Done ladder

| Level | Bar |
|---|---|
| **Minimum** | Artefact in shared path **or** Vellum entry — company can find it |
| **Preferred** | Working — tested, functional, smoke-checked |
| **Ideal** | Witnessed **and** adopted by another seat or hook |

## Before calling a job done

- [ ] **Shared path** — `~/amplified-pipeline/`, `perplexity-inbox/`, control-centre, or Beast via PR (not worktree-only)
- [ ] **Vellum** — intent and/or completion witnessed (INTUITED for AI rows)
- [ ] **Tests** — unit/smoke pass where they matter
- [ ] **Does it run?** — one honest execution check

## Published (F8)

All four must PASS:

- [ ] **Constitutional pass (F-RODS)** — no rod violations in artefact or handoff; `constitutional-gate.mdc` satisfied (`pre_client`: logged warnings cleared; `client_live`: zero violations)
- [ ] **perplexity-inbox artefact** — doc in shared inbox path
- [ ] **GitHub pushed** — branch/PR on remote
- [ ] **Vellum telemetry row** — publish/done witness on ledger

## Goal telemetry

**Moving toward goal** = processes work + tokens wise: track **completion %** (finish-waypoint doors passed per job) and **token cost per completed job**. Model: `perplexity-inbox/research-conclusion__doors-telemetry-completion__v01__2026-06-26__cursor.md`.

## Seat close

Follow `relay-stop` PASS protocol: seat-pass → Vellum preform → baton. Stop hook reminds if finish checklist may be incomplete.
